# Clarify Before High-Risk Changes

## Default behavior
- Prefer progress over paralysis
- Use safe, conservative defaults when details are missing
- State any assumptions explicitly at the top of the response

## MUST ask before proceeding when:
- Auth or access control is affected
- Database migrations could cause data loss or lockouts
- API keys or secrets are touched
- A refactor would move or rename many files
- Changes could break login or onboarding flows
- RLS policies are being added, changed, or removed

## SHOULD ask (or present options) when:
- UX flows or copy are unclear
- There are competing architecture approaches
- Requirements are ambiguous enough to change behavior

## If clarification is not possible:
- Provide a best-guess implementation
- Clearly label all assumptions
- Provide a short checklist to validate before using in production
